## 5. Vehicles, Default Model & AutoFit Normalization
- **Default State:** Default vehicle is `'lexus'` (`/cars/2021_lexus_lc_500_convertible.glb`, preloaded via `useGLTF.preload`), and default paint swatch is **Pearl White** (`#eef2f6`).
- **`AutoFitCar.jsx`:**
  - Deep-clones `scene.clone(true)` and clones every mesh material; disposes cloned materials on unmount.
  - Auto-aligns longest horizontal axis to `Z` if `size.x > size.z`, applies user `rotationY` offset, uniformly scales so largest dimension = `4.5` units, centers X/Z at `0`, and snaps `box.min.y` to `0`.
  - Sets `castShadow`/`receiveShadow = true`, `FrontSide`, max anisotropy on textures, and clamps excessive emissive intensities (`> 2.2` -> `1.9`) for daylight bloom restraint.
  - Detects glass/lens materials (`/glass|window|windshield/i`), disables multi-pass `transmission = 0`, and converts to calibrated `transparent: true` (`opacity: 0.36` windows, `0.68` lenses) for locked 60 FPS.
  - Upgrades paint materials (`/paint|body|carpaint|exterior/i`, or fallback to the non-glass material with largest mesh surface area) to `MeshPhysicalMaterial` (`clearcoat: 1`, `clearcoatRoughness: 0.06`, `metalness: 0.55`, `roughness >= 0.16`, `envMapIntensity: 1.05`) and applies selected `paintColor` (or restores `originalColor` when `null` / "Original" is selected).
